---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

const pageName = "Daniel Checketts"
---

<BaseLayout pageTitle={pageName}>
	<div class="bg-white/20 backdrop-blur-md border border-white/20 shadow-lg rounded-lg">
		<section
			id="welcome-banner"
			class="flex flex-col items-center gap-5 mb-10 md:grid md:grid-cols-2">

			<div
				id="welcome-banner-content"
				class="flex flex-col items-center">
				<div id="image-card" class="flex flex-col items-center">
					<img
						src="/img/daniel-checketts-2025.jpg"
						alt="Photo of Daniel Checketts"
						class="size-32 md:size-64 aspect-square rounded-full object-cover"
					/>
					<span class="">Me, Circa Late 2025</span>
				</div>

				<div id="welcome-banner-message" class="md:col-start-2">
					<span class="">Welcome!</span>
					<h1 class="">Hi, my name is Daniel Checketts, and I love writing code.</h1>
					<a href="/learn" class="rounded-full bg-emerald-600 text-white py-2 px-4">Start Learning</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section id="about" class="">
			<div class="space-y-4">
				<p class="">Computers have always been in my DNA—my dad graduated from BYU-Idaho in Computer Information Technology and programmed throughout my childhood. While middle and high school computer classes didn't quite capture my imagination, everything changed when I arrived at BYU-I myself.</p>
				<p class="">In an Intro to Programming course, I fell in love with Python. The class taught simple concepts like loops and logic gates, gave us a desired outcome, and granted us unlimited freedom to achieve it. That open-ended puzzle-solving hooked me.</p>
				<p class="">My path wasn't entirely linear; educational hardships initially pushed me away from my dad's exact degree track. However, while serving a mission for The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints, I found clarity. My mission gave me perspective on what I truly valued in my education, alongside unique opportunities to serve others using my technical instincts. For instance, when a temporary bug in Facebook Messenger began distorting shared links to vital tools like Google Forms and Sheets, I was able to help my friends by manually decrypting the broken links, translating the scrambled hexadecimal values into ASCII characters to recover the usable URLs.</p>
				<p class="">Today, I am pursuing my BS in Web Design &amp; Development.</p>
			</div>
		</section>
	</div>

		<section id="project-showcase" class="">
			<h2 class="section-heading">Projects</h2>
			<ul class="">
				<li class="">
					<a href="https://github.com/dchecketts/dchecketts.github.io" class="">
						<div class="">
							<h3 class="">Personal Website</h3>
							<p class="">This site, built with Astro, Tailwind, and HTMX.</p>
						</div>
					</a>
				</li>

				<li class="">
					<a href="https://github.com/dchecketts/vite-site-template" class="">
						<div class="">
							<h3 class="">Vite Site Template</h3>
							<p class="">A starter template for quickly spinning up sites.</p>
						</div>
					</a>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>
</BaseLayout>